message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "estimator-crossover-hardware: Sim-to-Silicon test of the estimator crossover on real hardware"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Agarwal
    given-names: Vaishvi
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
# Placeholder: the repository has not been published yet. Fix the URL if it differs.
repository-code: "https://github.com/vaishvi-agarwal/estimator-crossover-hardware"
abstract: >-
  Firmware (ESP32, Arduino), analysis code and test protocol for testing on
  real hardware whether the estimator crossover found in simulation survives
  real sensor noise: a Kalman filter, an innovation-gated Kalman filter, a
  2-mode IMM and a GRU estimator track a pendulum measured by a VL53L0X
  time-of-flight sensor, under proximity-coupled Gilbert-Elliott burst faults
  (inflated-variance, frozen and blended), physically caused faults, and real
  sensor lock-ups and latch-ups recovered by a protection circuit. Status:
  code complete; hardware validation pending. No results are included yet.
keywords:
  - state estimation
  - Kalman filter
  - interacting multiple model
  - GRU
  - fault tolerance
  - Gilbert-Elliott model
  - burst faults
  - single-event effects
  - ESP32
  - VL53L0X
references:
